From 0cf90614c2e6165f35853c261fdebdccd9b3926a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 17:18:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(release): adopt the #1027 VpsJournalMetrics interface in
 the VPS bridge, gated by the pinned driver

ubiquity/ai.ubq.fi#1027 (e50c298b) changed the bridge-facing interface of
ops/vps-release-metrics.ts. A driver re-pinned past it made
new VpsJournalMetrics(...) throw in checkedOptions, so every VPS release
was refused (sentinel#150).

The bridge now reads the interface from the owner-pinned, hash-verified
metrics module itself:
- window shape (ai.ubq.fi 21e4a2a9, the pin today): composed exactly as
  before, and the controller keeps its per-slot gap rule.
- joined shape (#1027): the bridge passes all five options. Retention and
  cipher come from the owner's telemetry capability. The context is read
  from committed release state: it binds the unique monitoring operation
  and re-reads a saved checkpoint at its own revision. Storage is the
  pinned tree's createVpsJoinFileStorage, and the deadline is the run
  deadline. Journal reads go through the bounded (args, limits, cwd)
  runner. The controller gets metricsWork: one beginTick per monitoring
  run before sampling, exact 30 s slots, and a wait (not a restart) on a
  slot that is still collecting. Acceptance also waits while a baseline
  slot is collecting.
- any other shape, or a joined driver without owner telemetry, is
  unavailable.

Before evaluating any module, the loader refuses a driver, metrics or
join-storage graph that names a bun: module. At e50c298b the driver and
the join storage both reach ops/deploy-lock.ts (bun:ffi). Such a pin is
still refused, now with the reason "trusted VPS driver needs a host that
can load Bun-only modules", until the driver offers a Deno-loadable lock.

tests/host/vps-release-driver-interface_test.ts pins the interface. It
runs the exact upstream bytes through the real loader; they are vendored
as .txt fixtures and checked against their Git blob ids. The controller
test drives the real #1027 metrics to acceptance through the composed
host.

No state field, bridge stdout code or result shape changes.

